        body: `<ol><li>Join the intended channel or an accepted private call and start its camera or screen-share control.</li><li>For a screen share, select a screen or window in the capture picker. Choose a resolution and frame rate that your connection and viewers can handle.</li><li>Choose <strong>No audio</strong>, <strong>Shared application</strong>, or <strong>System audio</strong> intentionally. When using application audio, select a window and enable audio in the system picker.</li><li>Confirm the share. Check what is visible before displaying personal windows, notifications, or credentials.</li><li>Use <strong>Change quality</strong> on a running channel share to adjust resolution and frame rate without reopening the picker. Stop sharing when finished.</li></ol><p>Application audio depends on the capture runtime and may include other windows from the same application. If application-only capture cannot be confirmed, video can start without audio and a notification explains the fallback. System audio is shared only when explicitly selected.</p><p>Current camera and screen shares upload one selected encoding. Viewers receive the same source quality; a slower viewer may need the sender to lower the settings. Selected resolution and actual delivered frame rate are different measurements.</p>`,
