        id: 'sign-in', title: 'Sign in or link from a trusted device',
        body: `<p>The connection screen offers the sign-in methods supported by the current server. A registered passkey can authorize a new device through the browser’s passkey prompt. Passkeys require a supporting browser and platform.</p><ol><li>On an existing desktop session, open <strong>Connections → PWA / Mobile login</strong>. Check that the PWA host shown really belongs to the server you are connected to.</li><li>Open the provided link, scan its QR code, or enter its hidden one-time code in the PWA.</li><li>Compare the two-digit verification code shown on the two devices and check that the request belongs to the device you intend to add.</li><li>Approve the request on the existing trusted device. Keep the PWA open while it waits for that decision.</li><li>If the code expires or the request is denied, start a new link. Do not approve an unexpected device request.</li></ol><p>After approval, this browser connects with its own registered device identity. When offered, save a passkey under <strong>You</strong> for a later sign-in. Guest access appears only when the server allows guest login; a server join password may still be required.</p><p>Use <strong>Devices &amp; passkeys</strong> on the desktop or the device list under You in the PWA to review the new device. Where confirmation is required, compare its fingerprint and confirm it before sending it direct messages. <strong>Copy recent history</strong> can transfer readable direct-message records from a confirmed existing device, with a chosen time range. This copies records rather than old encryption sessions or keys; the privacy guide explains the transfer’s limits.</p>`,
